**Options depending on the list:**

| Option | Cost | Complexity | Condition |
|---|---|---|---|
| Packer outputs a **managed image** (`Microsoft.Compute/images`) and the VMSS boots from it | Image storage only | Low | Only if `images` is on the list |
| Ask PwC to allow `Microsoft.Compute/galleries` (+ `galleries/images`, `galleries/images/versions`) | Image storage | Low (one SR line) | Closest to the GCP golden image flow, with versioned rollback |
| Skip images: VMSS from a base image plus a cloud-init install at boot | None | High, and slow scale-out | ⚠️ Drops the no-startup-download design you chose on GCP |

**Recommendation (provisional):** gallery via SR if PwC will allow it, since versioned image history is what the rollback step uses. If `images` is already allowed, a managed image is a fine interim that needs no SR. Choose after seeing the list.

⚠️ **Rollback weaker with managed images:** you keep previous images by name, not versions. Keep the last 3 and don't delete the current one's predecessor.

